{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01UTafsivnwGiag6DxYXKtJN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a personal productivity + R&D mission-control system built for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (single folder, no syncing). Grounded claims:\n\n- **It's a markdown-backed task/project manager.** Plain-text files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, `CANCELLED.md`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`) are the source of truth â€” no database. Tasks move through a lifecycle: active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved â†’ restored.\n\n- **It ships as a local web app.** `anchor_gui.py` is a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders an interactive dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, writing changes straight back to the markdown. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` (`nssm restart anchor` to bounce it). `anchor.py` is a CLI mirror of the same logic that also emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It has grown a layered \"R&D control surface\" (v2â†’v3â†’v4) for trio-driven development.** Each project gets a window/cockpit that runs the skill trio â€” **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman** â€” and tracks the work as *sessions* with cached, grounding-validated summaries, per-lane doc roles, and cost/tokens/time rollups.\n\n- **v4 \"Project Cockpit\" is the current state â€” built and merged to master (commit `38fd70e`, 2026-06-13).** Lanes (Research/Planning/Build/Deliverables/Grass) render as status-light tiles that expand into inline panels stacking a summary over a **real ConPTY terminal** (xterm.js over WebSocket/SSE). It adds a Claudeâ†”Gemini engine toggle, a grass idea board with promote-to-lane, type-aware deliverable launch, and the Ghost World Labs branding masthead.\n\n- **It's deliberately dependency-light.** Python 3.8+ stdlib only, with **one declared exception**: optional `pywinpty` for the ConPTY terminals (lazy import, in `pty_manager.py` only, `pip install .[terminal]`), degrading gracefully if absent. `distro.py` enforces this with an import scan.\n\n- **It self-tests daily.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5:00 AM via Task Scheduler â€” parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server, walks every endpoint and the fully-stubbed v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (never touching the live `:8777` service or real data), and writes a dated report to `health_reports/`.\n\nIn short: a single-user, markdown-native productivity dashboard that has evolved into a local mission-control for running and remembering AI-agent-driven R&D projects."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4308,"cache_read_input_tokens":45292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4308,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e99eb17c-acaf-4227-8cb9-12ac4ed8e01d","uuid":"1676c929-6bca-40fd-a9b6-8fb55af2a13c","request_id":"req_011Cc1JMXmvBcGGSGDeLVVir"}
